---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const base = '/participation-nd-ballot-history/20261107-01/';
type Counts = { ballots_by_year: Record<string, number>;
	reported_ballot_count_change_since_2024: number; reported_ballot_count_change_since_2022: number };
type County = Counts & { county_name: string };
const review: { statewide: Counts; counties: County[] } =
	JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}history.json`, 'utf8'));
const number = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const change = (value: number) => `${value > 0 ? '+' : ''}${number(value)}`;
---

<section id="participation-nd-history" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="nd-history-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Administrative ballot counts · county comparison</p>
		<h2 id="nd-history-title">North Dakota: presidential and midterm participation</h2>
		<p>Official 2022 and 2024 ballot totals alongside the <strong>unofficial 2026 snapshot</strong>
			updated November 5, 2026 at 01:30 UTC. These are reported ballot-count changes,
			<strong>not measured prior-voter drop-off or switching</strong>, and not an estimate of final 2026 turnout.</p>
	</header>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="North Dakota statewide ballot counts">
		<table>
			<caption>Statewide general-election ballots. Midterm-to-midterm and presidential-to-midterm
				comparisons are separate; candidate votes are not substituted for ballots.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Geography</th><th scope="col">2022 official</th>
				<th scope="col">2024 official</th><th scope="col">2026 snapshot</th>
				<th scope="col">Change vs. 2022</th><th scope="col">Change vs. 2024</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody><tr data-nd-state>
				<th scope="row">North Dakota</th>
				{['2022', '2024', '2026'].map(year =>
					<td data-nd-year={year}>{number(review.statewide.ballots_by_year[year])}</td>)}
				<td data-nd-change="2022">{change(review.statewide.reported_ballot_count_change_since_2022)}</td>
				<td data-nd-change="2024">{change(review.statewide.reported_ballot_count_change_since_2024)}</td>
			</tr></tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<details class="explorer-notes" id="nd-history-counties">
		<summary>All 53 county ballot comparisons</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="North Dakota county ballot counts">
			<table>
				<caption>Exact source county-name matches. Historical county totals are sums of complete
					native precinct rows, not independent county controls. No cross-year precinct match is claimed.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">County</th><th scope="col">2022 official</th>
					<th scope="col">2024 official</th><th scope="col">2026 snapshot</th>
					<th scope="col">Change vs. 2022</th><th scope="col">Change vs. 2024</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{review.counties.map(row => <tr data-nd-county={row.county_name}>
					<th scope="row">{row.county_name}</th>
					{['2022', '2024', '2026'].map(year =>
						<td data-nd-year={year}>{number(row.ballots_by_year[year])}</td>)}
					<td data-nd-change="2022">{change(row.reported_ballot_count_change_since_2022)}</td>
					<td data-nd-change="2024">{change(row.reported_ballot_count_change_since_2024)}</td>
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<p>The source contains 398 reporting units in 2022, 385 in 2024 and 358 in this 2026
		snapshot. Matching county names does not establish a fixed-person cohort, analytical
		boundary overlay or comparable precinct boundaries. No new map, demographic turnout rate,
		individual drop-off, returning-voter identity or candidate switching is inferred.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Source clocks, definitions and complete reproduction</summary>
		<p>The <a href="https://www.sos.nd.gov/elections/election-results">North Dakota Secretary of State archive</a>
			declares the historical turnout pages. Their native update clocks are November 29, 2022
			at 2:43:07 PM and April 21, 2026 at 1:33:23 PM for the 2024 election, with no supplied timezone.
			The current source is election 348, revision v75; its November 5 UTC clock is not a certification
			or final-count statement.</p>
		<p>Historical “Eligible Voters” means estimated residents aged 18+, not registered voters,
			a voting-eligible population or a fixed eligible cohort. Those native values remain in the
			download but are not used for rates. Historical county IDs are portal ordinals, not FIPS;
			current location IDs remain separate. Existing Morton and Towner mapping caveats remain.</p>
		<p>The complete archive includes every selected precinct ballot count, all county and statewide
			controls, election identities, status and source clocks, native source URLs and hashes,
			qualification, exact code and tests. It reproduces offline from these complete selected facts.
			Re-running the initial native extraction separately requires the pinned originals;
			copyrighted site markup, unrelated contests and personal records are not mirrored.
			This analysis is not endorsed by the source.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete North Dakota ballot inputs + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}history.json`} download>North Dakota county comparison + qualifications (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>North Dakota archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-nd-history { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
